</given-names></name></person-group><source>Oral literature in Africa</source><year>1970</year><publisher-name>Oxford, Clarendon Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leslau</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><source>Bibliography of the Semitic languages of Ethiopia</source><year>1946</year><publisher-name>Wiley Publishers, New York</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pound</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><source>Ethiopian music, an introduction</source><year>1968</year><publisher-name>Oxford University Press, Oxford</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kebede</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>Roots of black music</source><year>1982</year><publisher-name>Prentice-Hall Inc., New Jersey</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Elbourne</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A mirror of man? Traditional music as a reflection of society</article-title><source>The Journal of American Folklore</source><year>1976</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>463</fpage><lpage>468</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/539297</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lomax</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Folksong style and culture-Washington</article-title><source>American Association for Advancement of Science</source><year>1968</year></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Merriam</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Bascom W, Herskovits M</surname></name></person-group><article-title>African music</article-title><source>continuity and change in African cultures</source><year>1959</year><publisher-name>Chicago: University of Chicago Press</publisher-name><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>86</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Debalke</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ethiopian Music and Musical instruments</article-title><source>Ethiopian Herald</source><year>1967</year><publisher-name>Addis Ababa</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sarosi</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><source>Melodic pattern in the folk music of the Ethiopian peoples Proceedings of the third International Conference of Ethiopian studies</source><year>1970</year><volume>1</volume><publisher-name>Addis Ababa. Institute of Ethiopain Studies</publisher-name><fpage>280</fpage><lpage>287</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mondon-vidailhet</surname><given-names>FMC</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Lavignac A, de la Laurencie L</surname></name></person-group><source>The Ethiopian Music Encyclopaedia of Dictionary of Music</source><year>1922</year><publisher-name>1 ere partie, Paris: C. Delagrave</publisher-name><fpage>3179</fpage><lpage>3196</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kebede</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Music of Ethiopia: its development and cultural setting</source><year>1971</year><publisher-name>Ph.D. dissertation, Wesleyan University</publisher-name></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>